IntegrationGuard reads publicly available data about the repositories you
already have installed:

  HACS data endpoints   https://data-v2.hacs.xyz
                        The store index HACS itself uses. No token, no
                        account, and the same data your HACS already fetches.
  GitHub REST API       https://docs.github.com/rest
                        Only public repository metadata, and only for
                        repositories you installed. Optional: without a token
                        the public rate limit applies.

HACS is a separate project by Joakim Sørensen and its contributors:
https://github.com/hacs/integration

Third-party services IntegrationGuard can deliver notifications through —
Telegram, Pushover and ntfy — are operated by their respective owners.
IntegrationGuard only talks to their public APIs with credentials you supply.
Their terms of service and rate limits apply:

  Telegram Bot API   https://core.telegram.org/bots/api
  Pushover           https://pushover.net/api
  ntfy               https://docs.ntfy.sh

